// Title: Suspicious Use of CSharp Interactive Console
// Sigma ID: a9e416a8-e613-4f8b-88b8-a7d1d1af2f61
// Status: test | Level: high
// Author: Michael R. (@nahamike01)
// Date: 2020-03-08 | Modified: 2022-07-14
// ATT&CK: execution, stealth, T1127
// Description: Detects the execution of CSharp interactive console by PowerShell
// False positives:
//   - Possible depending on environment. Pair with other factors such as net connections, command-line args, etc.
// References:
//   - https://redcanary.com/blog/detecting-attacks-leveraging-the-net-framework/
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/process_creation/proc_creation_win_csi_use_of_csharp_console.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.

DeviceProcessEvents
| where FolderPath endswith "\\csi.exe" and (InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\powershell.exe" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\pwsh.exe" or InitiatingProcessFolderPath endswith "\\powershell_ise.exe") and ProcessVersionInfoOriginalFileName =~ "csi.exe"
